  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 125 PM MDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nBy Wednesday, guidance appears to be coming into better agreement \nwith a large dry slot moving east within the base of the larger \nupper level low circulation. A large band of wrap around precip is \nshown pivoting slowly east across northern NM. Additional precip \nmay push 1\", especially on northern and western-facing slopes. \nRiver flooding may peak Wednesday or Thursday in the wake of the \nexiting storm system. \n\nFolks are strongly advised to stay away from rivers and arroyos \nas banks can give way several feet away from fast-flowing water. \nLarge areas of standing water may form in low-lying areas and \nlow-water crossings may be inundated with high water and deep \nmud.\n\nThe rest of the forecast period from Thursday to Friday is likely to \nfeature decreasing humidity and warming temps as a ridge attempts to \nbuild over the region. Areas of fog may occur for several nights in \nthe wake of this system given saturated soils.",
